# REQUIRES: python-api, openmm
# Tunable parameters (D213) against independent references on
# the dipeptide in water: the energies at new charges, per-type sigma and
# epsilon, a constant of a pair term, and the parameters of a tuple term
# against OpenMM 8.6.1 (Reference platform) and NumPy sums; the correction
# for the dispersion at the new sigma and epsilon against its formula; and
# central differences of the energy in a tunable constant of a pair term
# against the derivative of `observe` (D189) of mdir run at the same
# positions, with the tail and the estimate of the shift (D209, D210).
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/python_tunable.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide oracle mdir %t | FileCheck %s
# CHECK: oracle: U(theta0)
# CHECK: oracle: U(theta1)
# CHECK: oracle: U(theta1) - U(theta0)
# CHECK: oracle: the correction for the dispersion at the new sigma and epsilon
# CHECK: derivative: central differences
# CHECK: oracle passed
